Skill add_ai_task_delivery {
  label: 'Add delivery to an AI task'
  description: "Use when an AI task's result goes by email or to Slack, for a new task, this chat's draft or a named task. Settles the destination and the attachment. Typical phrasings: “email me the summary every Friday”, “post it in #sales-alerts”, “attach the chart”. Loaded by create_ai_task for any email or Slack destination. Do not use for a send right now, or for a result that stays in Holistics."
  invocation: 'auto'
  disabled: H.git.is_production
  content: @md
    # Add delivery to an AI task

    Settle who gets the result and what comes with it, then write both into the brief. Runs send on their own: add no disclaimer.

    ## Resolve the destination

    - An email address, a Slack channel or "email me" (`${H.current_user.h_email}`) is settled.
    - For a group, ask "Which email addresses? Type them."
    - For Slack, ask "Which Slack channel? Type its exact name." If none is named, ask again or offer email. Never borrow a channel from another task.
    - Several destinations are fine. Write each.
    - Give no recommendation on these cards.

    ## Resolve the attachment

    Whenever the result is sent, ask one `ask_user` card: "What should come with the result?" Skip it only when the user named an attachment or said none.

    - Options: "A chart of the result (recommended)", "The <name> dashboard", "No attachment".
    - For the dashboard, search the task's data (`*.page.aml`, every folder level) and name the best match. If none fits, offer "A dashboard (tell me which)".
    - A named file type ("as a PDF") is settled.
    - Keep the best pick of the other kind for the draft report's button: "Attach the <name> dashboard instead" or "Attach a chart instead". No button when nothing is attached.

    ## Write it into the brief

    - **At a glance:** Sends to = each destination ("Email · you@x.com", "Slack · #sales", joined by "; "). Condition = the rule in plain words, when sending only on a condition. Attachment = "None", "Viz · PNG", "Dashboard · <name> · PNG" or the file type.
    - **Steps:** fill {Condition} (exclusive branches, each naming its destinations; it never writes the message), {Attach} (export as PNG) and {Deliver} (one message per destination, with the attachment).
    - **Subject:** write it word for word in {Deliver}. Email "<task label> · <period dates>" in digits ("Mar 4 – 10"; none for a task without a period). Slack "<task label>". Never "Last Week" for the dates.
    - Add an acceptance criterion only when the destination or condition changes what a run must produce.
  ;;
}
